WEBVTT

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.750
"Koto Club"

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.040
"#15    Becoming Aware"
I came in for some reason even though
we don't have morning practice today.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.580
We lost yesterday...

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:00.330
...to a school whose performance
we didn't even hear.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.540
You guys can become even better.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.290
Hm? It's not locked?

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.040
Ah...

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.500
Why are <i>you </i>here?

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.830
Why are <i>you </i>here? I told you guys
there's no practice today.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.370
Yeah, we know.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.080
But we've practiced koto
day in and day out all summer.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.120
So we don't know what else
to do with ourselves now.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.370
Guys...

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.830
Jeez... This is no different
from any other day after all.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.790
Our next competition
is the national qualifier, right?

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.200
Which piece are we playing?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.250
We can practice "Kuon" more,
or maybe learn a new piece?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.910
Wha...? You guys are all here?
Don't you have anything else to do?

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.120
Mr. Takinami?! Why're you here?

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.410
Never mind.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.160
Well then, here.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.160
"For School Festival"
Sheet music?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.910
It's a medley of a bunch of pieces
that are popular these days.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.700
Your next performance is
the school festival in September.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.950
Play this piece for that.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.790
What?

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:06.450
You guys have a serious lack of
experience performing in public.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.370
As a first step, grab any chance
to gain experience.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.830
Say something.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.790
You sound like a club advisor.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.790
That's because I <i>am </i>your club advisor.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:18.950
Suzu...!

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:24.370
But an arrangement of popular pieces?
Where'd you find sheet music like this?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.450
I didn't. I wrote it.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.200
Oh, that makes sense.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.790
It even has koto notation written in.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:31.700
Huh?!

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.500
You wrote it?!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.790
Y-You mean <i>you </i>wrote it?!

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.700
Who else could it be?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.950
But it's a music piece.
And it even has koto notation!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.910
I thought you had no
experience with the koto!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.410
After two years of being a koto club advisor,

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.200
I can at least read and write a koto score.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.080
Oh, is that right?

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.950
Wow...

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.200
If even a non-koto player like him can do it,
maybe we can already do it, too.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.580
No way!

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.910
You guys really are idiots!

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.750
Mr. Takinami, what on earth...?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.410
Enough about me. More importantly,
that score has three parts.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:06.370
First and second koto and the 17-string.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.250
I made the 17-string part simpler.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:12.620
So this time, instead of Hozuki,
you play it, Adachi.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:14.120
What? Me?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.700
You have a good sense of rhythm and power,
so you're probably suited for it.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.250
There's a little less than
a month till the school festival.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.700
We've got enough time.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.700
So we'll also decide on the piece
for the qualifier during this time.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.700
I'll look for one, too, but Hozuki,

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:33.160
you're more familiar with koto music,
so let me know if you find something.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.120
Well then... practice that piece, okay?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.370
What? Huh? What the heck is going on?
What happened to Suzu?

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:45.290
I-I don't know.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:45.660
"For School Festival"

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:46.830
"For School Festival"
But...

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.160
And one more thing.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.750
Make sure you finish your summer assignments,

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.910
or you'll attract the vice principal's
attention again,

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.080
and then you might not be able
to perform at the school festival.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.580
What assignments?

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.200
We had assignments?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.580
Eeeek.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:08.700
You don't have to worry, Takezo.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:12.660
We've got the ultimate secret weapon.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.790
What?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.620
"Math I"
Thanks for helping us again!

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:20.080
I'm sorry that I tagged along, Takaoka.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.410
No, actually, I appreciate it.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.410
I can't handle them all by myself,
so it'd be great

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.660
if you could help me teach them.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.790
At any rate, I didn't expect Takaoka
to be their secret weapon.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.000
Tetsuki is super smart.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.040
It's thanks to him that we
were able to get into Tokise.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.080
He got the highest score on the entrance exam.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.160
What?!

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.290
Okay then. Let's start with math.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.830
Alrighty.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:45.620
"Math I"

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.580
Hey, Tetsuki.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:56.120
It looks like the math textbook
isn't doing well right now,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.540
so let's work on a different subject.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.950
It's your head that's not doing well.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.500
"30 minutes later"

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.620
Math is scary. Math is scary.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.000
I'm hungry.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.000
That's too soon!

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.910
I mean, what's the deal with X and Y?!

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.790
Aren't they trying too hard
to hide their identities?

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:14.870
They should live more confidently!
Are they shy or what?!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.000
We just aren't that into you, you know!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:18.410
--I-It certainly isn't easy to teach them.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.080
--The hell with X!
--I-It certainly isn't easy to teach them.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.450
I wonder how Takaoka does it...

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.000
--Stupid idiots! What's their problem?!

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.540
--So you guys are just gonna
turn your backs on X and Y, huh?
--Stupid idiots! What's their problem?!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.040
--So you guys are just gonna
turn your backs on X and Y, huh?
--Stop messing with us!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.910
--So you guys are just gonna
turn your backs on X and Y, huh?
--I don't get it anymore!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.500
T-Turn our backs on...?

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:38.580
They've been forced to conceal
their identities since birth

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.200
and live in solitude, unable to reveal
their true selves to anyone.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.120
And you guys just turn your backs on them,
saying, "Who cares?"

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.620
Poor things.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.750
Since birth...

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.750
In solitude...

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.000
Poor X...! Poor Y...!

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.700
We're sorry!
We're not gonna leave you alone!

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:02.370
I'm not gonna give up on you!

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.790
What?!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:07.830
Mr. Tetsu! Tell me how I can
save X from her solitude!

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.580
Mr. Takezo! Please teach me this!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.500
It's kinda nice... to spend time
like this for a change.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.830
All right! We're done with English, too!

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:30.750
Tetsu.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.660
What?

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.700
I'm hungry. Dinner!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:38.410
Let me help you.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.000
Ah... Thank you very much.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.000
Well then, could you wash those vegetables?

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.290
Okay.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:54.160
At any rate, you really are smart.
You're good at teaching, too.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.660
Yeah?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.950
Yeah. Couldn't you have gone
to a better high school?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.910
Why did you come to Tokise?

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.540
Well...

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.750
No reason in particular.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.330
It's close to my house, and it seemed
more fun at Tokise, so...

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.910
That's all.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.040
I see.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.950
Hey, four-eyes!

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:16.620
If you're in the kitchen, too,
there's no one to teach us!

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.500
What? Ahh, sorry.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.660
You're still calling him "four-eyes"?

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.750
Shut up.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.290
Oh, but there was one time
when you called me "sir."

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.200
What?

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.950
Though it was a while back. Remember?

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.000
You wanna get hurt?

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.500
But well, with all said and done...

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.500
If there's something you
can't solve on your own,

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.410
let's all think about it together!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.830
Mizuhara. Don't feel like you
have to rush yourself.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.450
...I feel like you really are
the club president.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.540
What?

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.830
It was a long time ago,

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.830
but like the time like when Hozuki
told us about her situation...

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:54.200
I... have been excommunicated
from the Hozuki school.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.910
Hozuki...

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.660
Thank you for telling us!

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.330
It was probably what she wanted
to hear the most at that moment.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:07.200
It's incredible that you said
those words so promptly.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.040
I can't say things like that, so...

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.580
What? A-Are you crying?

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.160
No! It's the onion!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.870
You haven't even peeled it yet, though.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.450
Let's go back to studying already. Jeez...

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.160
I'll be fine, so please go help them.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.950
S-Sorry.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:31.910
Kurata.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.620
Thank you.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.370
What?

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.580
When Chika told me that he was
going to join the koto club,

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:42.450
I thought it'd be tough for him in many ways.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:47.120
I thought he'd be rejected by the club members.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.830
But I was wrong.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.540
Kurata.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:58.330
Thank you for preserving the only place
where he could get over his hardships.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.660
That's my line.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:13.120
Kudo is a new member of the koto club!

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.000
It's only natural that he'd be in the club room!

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.580
We're members of the same club, after all.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.500
I don't want to lose my precious friends
or the place I belong,

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.410
so we are going to play this piece
till the very end.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.410
I felt like I should tell you all this.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.120
What will you do?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.000
Will you quit?

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.370
Let's make this... our best performance yet!

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.700
Whoooa! It looks yummy!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:39.660
Thank you!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.120
Wow! It's yummy!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.660
Tetsuki's curry is the best curry.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.870
Thanks. Actually, I wanted
to let it stand about a day, but...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.830
I'll eat it again tomorrow.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.660
What? Are you guys staying over?

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.370
Is that a problem?

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.790
Well, it's not a problem, I guess.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.370
Seconds, please!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.830
That was fast.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:05.290
The son of Kaoru Takinami
and Tsukasa Yukimori?!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.410
So I heard.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.660
You know about them, Takezo?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.540
What?! You guys don't know them?!

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.080
He's a world-renowned conductor,
and she's a piano prodigy!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.290
Are they famous?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.370
They are. Even I know about them.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.580
Having them as his parents,
he must have quite a good ear for music.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.870
So someone like that, who's always
listened to super high-level music,

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.250
said our performance was good, huh?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.830
That makes me feel extra happy.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.750
I'm happy for you guys.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.410
All right! I'm getting fired up!

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.830
Let's hurry up and finish the assignments!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.250
Okay, then, Tetsuki.
Let's exchange assignments.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.830
How about I deck you instead?!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.540
"Impatient"
"The only one practicing
with a cardboard koto"

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.290
"September 1"

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.540
Completely healed!

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.580
Are you serious?! It's only been
two weeks or so, hasn't it?

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.790
Don't underestimate my healing power.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.410
If you aren't careful, you'll hurt it again.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.790
Oh? It's been a while since
the last time you wore hair down.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.750
Wh-What? Is that a problem?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.200
No, it doesn't matter either way.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.200
Is that so?

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.660
Why are you upset?

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:23.200
I'm not. This is how I usually am.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.700
Well, with a majority vote, it's now decided

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.450
"<i>Okonomiyaki  Takoyaki  </i>Waffles  Churros  Crêpes"
that we'll do a waffle booth
at the school festival!

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.700
And we're going to decide on
the roles now as well.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.750
I can't believe we're even on
the shopping team together.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.160
I'm sorry.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.370
Why are you apologizing?

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.080
Why do I, of all people,
have to be with boring people?

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.450
Hey, Miyu!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.410
What? You know, you've become
really mellow lately.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:58.080
You used to make fun of Kurata
by calling him Nadeshiko, too.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.000
I'm sorry.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.000
No problem at all.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.330
Why're you laughing?

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:15.370
Well, you've said harsher things
to my face, so...

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:19.870
Besides... I know what you're like now.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.160
So don't worry.

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:25.790
Oh... shoot...

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.830
I feel like...

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.660
...crying...

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:33.120
Hey, what's with that reaction?
Don't tell me you--

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.790
Saeki.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.910
Your ability to pick up
on things needs some work.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.500
Huh?! I don't wanna be told that
by a boring guy like you!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.120
You don't know what you should
or shouldn't say, either.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.370
You seriously piss me off!

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:49.450
A Japanese-style cafe?
Your class will be doing that?

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.500
Serving things like matcha au lait
and <i>hojicha </i>latte?

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.040
And strawberry <i>daifuku</i>!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.870
Strawberry <i>daifuku</i>?

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.080
Chika insisted and it became
part of the menu.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.450
Who has an idea for the menu?

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.200
Strawberry <i>daifuku</i>!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:08.120
The class got noisy, saying like,
"Kudo suggested strawberry <i>daifuku</i>?

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.790
How're we supposed to react to that?"

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.620
What about you guys' class?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.250
A classic--a haunted house!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.580
Anyhow, I could see the three of you
participating in the school festival,

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:22.200
but Chika, too? I'm surprised.
You'll perform, too, right?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.040
Yeah.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.080
Before I played it, I thought it was
probably a lame medley.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.000
But then, it was actually a super cool piece.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.450
Yeah. Not only are
Mr. Takinami's parents amazing,

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.790
but he's no ordinary person, either.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.120
The other day, too...

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:39.580
These are music CDs and DVDs that
I don't think you normally listen to.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.950
As a first step, listen to all of them.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.200
What?

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.080
This is an inordinate amount...

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.750
This is only a fraction
of what I carefully selected.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:52.750
The amount of music you guys come
in contact with is overwhelmingly small.

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.040
Listen to a variety of excellent
music as often as possible,

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.500
and learn various sounds and expressions.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.370
Absorb them into yourselves.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.500
Develop a great deal of musicality.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:07.330
When you do, playing the koto
will become a lot more fun.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.000
Well then, make sure you listen to them.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:12.330
Um, Mr. Takinami! You're not going
to help us with our performance?

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:15.120
After you finish those CDs and DVDs.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:20.290
So we've been listening to that
music all day long, every day.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.910
Sounds like you guys will get busy again.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.910
Don't feel so lonely, Tetsu.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.200
We'll make sure to go over
and eat with you sometimes.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.830
--Don't come.
--Ow!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.450
Anyhow, I was surprised earlier.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.080
I thought Kudo was scary,
but then, he likes strawberries?

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.410
When it was decided, he looked happy.
He's super cute!

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.870
C-Cute?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.790
Satowa. What's Kudo like during club?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:49.450
What? Wh-What's he like?
I think he's just normal...

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:53.040
There are more guys than girls
in the koto club, right?

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:55.290
Is there anyone you like, Satowa?

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.830
What?! N-No, there's no one like that!

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.080
Really?!

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:03.450
Hey, I got a boyfriend over the summer.
He's from another school.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.120
You did?! I envy you!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.290
Wh-What's this conversation?

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.080
Is this what girls normally talk about?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.250
I-I can't follow it at all.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.700
"Koto Nut" "Club Activity Nut"

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.120
"Koto Club"

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:20.540
Yeah, it's normal for the number
of couples to increase after summer.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.000
We're high-school girls in
the flower of youth after all.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.370
I didn't realize girls are like that.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:29.700
Hiro... Do you think I'm a little off?

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.450
I don't get those kinds of topics at all.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.330
Aww, you're so cute.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:37.160
It's okay. I like you
just the way you are, Hozy.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:44.700
I-Is there... someone... who, um... y-you like?

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:45.830
What?

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.750
There's no one.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.410
What was that pause for?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:52.290
S'up?!

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.750
Oh, Sane. Are you by yourself today?

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:58.290
Well, Mittsu and Kota are on cleaning duty,
so I left them behind.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.040
I wanted to practice sooner, so...

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.870
I get it. You're playing
the 17-string this time, so...

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.790
I feel a little pressure,

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.410
but I'm happy about
being entrusted with this.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:10.330
I feel like I'm being given some credit.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.450
So, I'm sorry to bother you again, Hozuki,

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:15.000
but please instruct me
on the 17-string today, too!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.370
I'll work you hard.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:17.620
Thanks!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:23.160
This atmosphere makes me feel comfortable.
It's more suited for me.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:28.580
Is there... someone... you like?

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:34.080
Focus! We're gonna go
to nationals for sure!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.790
I should follow Sane's example
and practice hard!

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:37.620
Hm?

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:41.830
Hey, shopping team! Can you go shopping?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.290
Here, this is the shopping list.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.410
Okay.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.290
Well then, shall we go?

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.290
What? Just the two of us?

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.620
The other two aren't around, so...

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.910
If you don't want to, I can go by myself.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:55.040
That's not what I meant.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:01.200
Hey, why am I feeling restless?

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.870
I don't get it.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.620
When I think about it, we've been
alone in his room before, right?

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.750
It's just shopping. A piece of cake.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:09.580
Hm?

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:11.750
Hiro?

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.580
What...? This voice...

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:20.410
Ah! I was right. It's you, Hiro!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:26.370
I heard you've been complaining
about me to your friends?

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.330
Hiro! I heard you've been harassing Minami

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:30.910
because you don't want her
to steal your man, right?

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.500
What's with that? You're the worst.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.080
What a coincidence! It's been a while, huh?

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:39.250
Mi... nami... Naoya...

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.200
Are they your friends, Kurusu?

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.120
Is he the guy you're dating now?

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.540
N-No.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.830
I still hear bad things about you.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.870
Are you still doing
the kind of stuff you did to us?

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.620
I didn't do anything to you two.

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:01.120
I told you that... so many times.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:07.000
You said that and never gave us
any word of apology.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Why do I...?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.200
Sorry, but we're in a hurry, so...

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:18.160
Let's go.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:25.750
You should be careful.
If you trust her, one day, you'll--

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:36.080
You needn't worry... since I'm
a better judge of people than you.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.620
Kurata... Kurata!

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.830
My hand... Hand!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.080
Ah, yeah. Sorry.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.790
U... Um...

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:02.450
Well then, let's go finish shopping.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.330
Oh, no...

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.370
Shoot...

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:13.040
My heart... Don't beat so loudly... Don't!

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:18.000
Hozuki, what're you making?

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.910
Wh-What am I making? Can't you tell?

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.910
The menu we'll put out outside our classroom.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.830
"Green Tea 150 yen"
"<i>Hojicha </i>150 yen"
"Matcha Latte 150"
Hmm...

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.290
What's this?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.950
Drawing of a teacup.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:30.870
And this?

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.200
S-Strawberry <i>daifuku</i>.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.540
Amazing...! You're such a great artist.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:44.040
What? Kudo laughed?!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.580
"Orange"

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:49.540
What're you doing?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.870
What? Ah...

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.000
N-Nothing.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:57.410
Really, what am I doing?

00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:00.660
Anyway, isn't this base board too distorted?

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.040
I got scrap wood, so...

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.080
I'll fix it for you. Give me the tool.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.540
Hey! A nail is sticking out there!

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:19.000
Whoa! S-Sorry!

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.450
Don't get it wrong! It was,
you know, that! An accident!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:24.080
I meant no harm!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:27.250
Well, I moved forward suddenly, so...

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:34.750
What? Hm? Why?

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.910
I-I'm sorry!

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.830
Ah... Hozuki...

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.700
I made her cry...

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:48.950
My face feels hot... What should I do?

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:54.080
It feels hot...

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.450
Look! Mine looks super scary!

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.540
Let's put more fake blood!

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:52.200
Next time, "Their Time."

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.500
"#16    Their Time"
